import QEC.Stabilizer.Framework.Symplectic.IndependentEquiv
import QEC.Stabilizer.Framework.Symplectic.SymplecticOrthogonal
import QEC.Stabilizer.Framework.Symplectic.SymplecticSpan
import QEC.Stabilizer.Framework.Symplectic.SymplecticImage
import QEC.Stabilizer.Framework.Symplectic.Presentation
import QEC.Stabilizer.Framework.Symplectic.WeightTwoInSpan
import QEC.Stabilizer.Framework.Symplectic.SupportLemmas
import QEC.Stabilizer.Framework.Symplectic.CentralizerStructure

/-!
# Symplectic view of stabilizer groups

Results connecting the binary-symplectic representation of Pauli operators
(`Foundations.BinarySymplectic`) to stabilizer groups and codes
(`Framework.Core`).

- `IndependentEquiv`: `listToSet` and `AllPhaseZero` for generator lists;
  linearly independent check-matrix rows give independent generators.
- `SymplecticSpan`: `sympSpan L`, the span of the check-matrix rows of a list;
  up to phase it is the subgroup generated by `L`, and independent commuting
  phase-zero generators do not generate `−I`.
- `SymplecticImage`: the symplectic image of a stabilizer group, on which the
  symplectic map is injective, so that `Nat.card S = 2 ^ rank`.
- `Presentation`: `StabilizerCode.Presentation`, a generator-list presentation
  of a code, and its soundness map `toCode` into `StabilizerCode`.
- `WeightTwoInSpan`: reduction of "every weight-two operator commuting with the
  generators lies in `sympSpan L`" to a finite enumeration.
- `SymplecticOrthogonal`: the symplectic form as a nondegenerate bilinear form,
  symplectic orthogonals, and the absence of weight-`w` logical operators when
  the weight-`w` part of the centralizer lies in `sympSpan L`.
- `SupportLemmas`: the support of `NQubitPauliOperator.set` and of Z-type and
  X-type operators.
- `CentralizerStructure`: the centralizer as the symplectic orthogonal of the
  symplectic image, and the classification of its elements for codes with one
  logical qubit.
-/
